 <test name="test I su ponte CH 1">
   
  <operation type="flush"></operation>
  
  <c>  parm1 is t-high parm2 is t-low . Current must be divided by 0.76277 in S16LE format</c>
  <c>  Consider measured mean current is 15.8 A (pick on the ADC is 31A) introducing 10% tolerance </c>
  <c>  then th = 17.6 and tl = 14.2 </c>
  <c>  th = 17698 -> 4522    tl = 14290 ->  37d2   </c>
  <c>  Note: when running this test, it might be that the ADC is takes a while to stabilize, so the test might fail. If this happens, just repeat the test.</c>
  <c>  If the test fails, it is possible to increase slightly the current on the power supply, e.g 0.5/0.8 A more.</c>
  
  <operation type="send" hex='1'>0x40 0xFF 0xFF 0x1c 0x22 0x45 0xd2 0x37 </operation> 
   <operation type="sleep">120</operation>
  <operation type="recvpassfail" hex="1"  reportfail="1">0xfe 0xff 0xff 0x8c 0x00 0x00</operation>
  
 </test>

